From 64da666dae5c85a94b8c27692c57bcd2502e7b74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:21:37 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 21/31] kcm_gamecontroller: Device page, list of controllers,
 live test view on its own sub-page

Page type: Device (docs/page-design.md). C++ (DeviceModel, Device, models, kcm pluginEnabled kcfg) unchanged. Not built yet.

Moved / renamed:
- Main page is the list of connected controllers (name, then type / controller type / connection as a subtitle); clicking one
  does kcm.push("Controller.qml", {deviceId}). The Device combo is gone (kcm_gamecontroller/Device).
- "Allow using as pointer and keyboard" switch (was a toolbar action) is a checkbox "Use controllers as pointer and
  keyboard" at the top with its ContextualHelpButton (pluginEnabled); the sleep/lock warning is an inline message under it
  (SleepWarning), now not tied to the old header slot. Empty state unchanged (NoControllers).
- Controller.qml (new): Device type / Controller type / Connection type as read-only FormLayout rows
  (DeviceType, ControllerType, ConnectionType), then Left/Right position widgets and the Buttons and Axes tables
  unchanged (LeftPosition, RightPosition, Buttons, Axes). Goes back to the list by itself if the controller is unplugged.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006 (order by use), HIG-057 (test view on a named sub-page).

Speed cause (devicemodel.cpp): the DeviceModel singleton arms a 2 s poll timer and a first poll after 100 ms; SDL_Init and device
opening run in that poll on the GUI thread, i.e. after the first frame, not in the constructor. The old page built both
tables, both position widgets and their models (updating every 100 ms) for the selected device up front; now they are only
created when a controller is opened. SDL_Init itself still runs on the GUI thread (not moved: needs a C++ thread change).
After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Unconfirmed: kcm.push with a relative QML name and an initial-properties map in this KCM (same call as kcm_activities); the
delegate reading model.id/model.text roles; Controller.qml picked up by kcmutils_add_qml_kcm's ui/* glob (it is). The
pluginEnabled checkbox has no SettingStateBinding: the KCM exposes the value as a property, not a config object. Not compiled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
